; SweK_Engine fbxIngest-selfcheck fixture -- hand-authored, original content, ASCII FBX 7.4.
; Not derived from any third-party asset -- written for this repository, zero licensing question.
; The same 2-bone skinned quad as fbxAnim.ascii.fbx (root at the origin, child offset (0,1,0), quad skinned
; with no blending), but BOTH bones now animate INDEPENDENTLY (root 0->90 degrees about X, child ALSO 0->90
; degrees about Y -- a second, separate rotation curve, its own axis, so a mesh that merely inherited root's
; motion would visibly differ from one that correctly tracks child's own combined motion), plus TWO plain,
; unskinned secondary meshes: "propMesh" (a small quad offset far from the rig) with NO parent-Model
; connection, so FBXLoader attaches it directly to the scene root -- unrelated to any bone; and "attachMesh"
; (a small unit quad) WITH a parent-Model connection to "child" -- a genuine bone attachment, e.g. a held
; item meant to track a wrist. Exercises normalizeFbxGroup()'s v5 mixed-skin-scope fix two ways: propMesh
; must stay exactly where authored (not drag with root's rotation, the v4 bug); attachMesh must track CHILD's
; own combined motion (root's rotation composed with child's own separate rotation) -- an adversarial review
; of the v5 fix's first draft named this second case as the more discriminating, not-yet-tested scenario,
; since a mesh that was still (incorrectly) bound to joint 0 alone would move differently from one correctly
; following its real parent bone whenever that bone has motion of its own beyond what it inherits from root.

